# system-details cli-json --------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Inferred from origin/main (unreleased). Decision 1 (a): hardn$
# system-details --output json, whose flag is unit (d)'s; the$
# document is output.Build's. On pkg/output's document, not$
# beside it: --output json is one flag with one contract$
# (docs/reference/output.md), mode "check" already means "read,$
# change nothing", host already holds the name and OS, and$
# wire.go's SchemaVersion comment lets a field be added without$
# a new version. So the nine fields, and one more, details, on$
# this form alone; result nothing-to-do, exit 0. logins holds$
# each account's answer. As a user other than root main()'s two$
# lines (cli-not-root) reach stdout first until unit (d) moves$
# them, and the output would not parse.$
$
